NEGRONI GPU memory (0402): who holds the wired IOKit memory, and the write-combined pool sized to the [ram] gpu region.
RedwoodGPU counts per client and in total: buffers of their own in wired kernel RAM, pool use, host imports (and
buffers left to a GPU that did not finish). The NEGRONI WIRED near/refused lines (0399) carry
"GPU RAM <MiB>, pool <used>/<size> MiB (full <n> times), host <MiB>; top (RAM+pool+host MiB) <3 clients>", each
client's close line its RAM/pool/host and its most. "RedwoodGPU: pool full ..." (first 4, then every 256th) when a
write-combined buffer falls back to wired kernel RAM. Pool: first fit from the lowest free page (in-use count, no
scan of the full start), never past the end of the RAM bank 0xa80000000; config negronigpu_pool=2048 (was 512).
Details: patches/xnu/README-gpu-kernel.md section 32, docs/notes.md section 91.

